@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: dl-007-cancelling-a-booking-refunds-the-full-total-before-the-rental-starts-and-nothing-after
+type: decision-log
+title: "Cancelling a booking refunds the full total before the rental starts and nothing after"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Context
+
+The desk needs to cancel bookings when customers' plans change. The request adds
+`cancel(bookingId, at)`, which cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`,
+the amount given back to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, and a booking
+can be cancelled only once.
+
+The request does not say how much is refunded. It does pass the time of cancellation, which only matters
+if the refund depends on when the customer cancels. The README says cancellations are not implemented yet.
+
+# Decision
+
+- `cancel(bookingId, at)` refunds the booking's full total when `at` is before the start of the rental.
+  When `at` is the start of the rental or later, the refund is `0`. The booking is cancelled either way.
+- `at` is a UTC instant written `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`, with an optional `.000` before the `Z`. Any minute
+  is allowed, since a customer may cancel at any time. Any other form is rejected.
+- Cancelling an unknown booking id throws. Cancelling a booking a second time throws.
+- A cancelled booking no longer blocks its equipment for `book` or `availability`. Its booking id is not
+  reused: the id counter does not go back.
+- The result is `{ bookingId, refund }`, with `refund` in integer euro cents.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- A customer who cancels before the rental starts gets the whole amount back. A customer who cancels once
+  it has started gets nothing, so the policy is strict and needs a decision from the school before it is
+  relied on.
+- Partial refunds, fees, and refunds after the rental has ended are not covered. Changing any of them is a
+  change of this decision.
+- Cancellation does not record when the refund was paid, since the module has no payment step.
