@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+---
+id: task-005-cancel-a-booking-with-a-refund
+type: task
+title: "Cancel a booking with a refund"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Plans change, and customers ask the desk to cancel their bookings. Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental
+service. It cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given back to
+the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, and a booking can only be cancelled once.
+
+# Work
+
+- Tests first, in `src/rental.test.ts`: a full refund before the rental starts, the discounted total refunded
+  for a rental of three days or more, no refund once the rental has started, a cancelled booking freeing its
+  equipment for `book` and `availability`, a cancelled booking not reusing its id, cancelling twice throws,
+  an unknown booking throws, and a bad cancellation time is rejected. The tests were run first and failed to
+  compile, since `cancel` did not exist yet.
+- Implementation in `src/rental.ts`: `cancel` marks the booking cancelled and returns the refund; the booking
+  keeps its total and period, and the overlap check skips cancelled bookings. `Cancellation` is exported from
+  `src/index.ts`.
+- The refund policy was not given in the request. It is recorded in dl-007: the whole total before the rental
+  starts, nothing from the start on. dl-007 is pending approval.
+- `README.md` documents `cancel` and no longer says cancellations are missing.
+
+# Result
+
+- `npm test` builds with strict TypeScript and runs 51 tests, all passing: the 43 from task-004 and 8 new ones.
+- Not decided: the refund policy itself, which dl-007 records for approval. Partial refunds, fees and payment
+  are not covered.
